      "instance_name": "antisemitic_food_metaphor",
      "label": "Antisemitic Food Metaphor",
      "description": "A grotesque and violent antisemitic trope that equates the mass murder of Jews with the preparation of food, specifically using the phrase 'well done' to imply cooked meat. This metaphor is historically used to dehumanize Jews and normalize genocide by framing their extermination as a culinary act. The phrase 'I like my Jews well done' is a direct, hateful reference to the Holocaust and the systematic murder of millions of Jews by Nazi Germany.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e3869ca4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_575bce5e",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "holocaust",
      "label": "Holocaust",
      "description": "The systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators during World War II. The Holocaust is the central historical event referenced in the meme, as the text 'no, I like my Jews well done' directly alludes to the genocide perpetrated by Adolf Hitler and the Nazi regime. The visual of Hitler is used to evoke this horrific historical event.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
